<section class="section about-grid">
  <div class="about-main">
    <p class="about-lead">The Spacesuits is a structured engineering archive covering US, Soviet, Russian and Chinese pressure garment programs. Built from primary sources — not aggregated listicles, not AI-generated content, not Wikipedia summaries in dark mode.</p>
    <h2 id="methodology" style="font-family:'Bebas Neue',sans-serif;font-size:2rem;letter-spacing:.04em;margin:2.5rem 0 1rem">Methodology</h2>
    <p>Every variant is documented against a normalized schema: pressure, mass, life support architecture, mission role, entry/donning method, key subsystem signatures, failure modes, and forward relevance. Data is sourced from primary engineering documents — NASA technical reports, OIG audit findings, and the primary published references for Soviet programs.</p>
    <h2 id="sources" style="font-family:'Bebas Neue',sans-serif;font-size:2rem;letter-spacing:.04em;margin:2.5rem 0 1rem">Primary Sources</h2>
    <ul class="sources-list">
      <li>Abramov, I.P. &amp; Skoog, A.I. — <em>Russian Spacesuits</em>, Springer Praxis, 2003</li>
      <li>Thomas, K.S. &amp; McMann, H.J. — <em>U.S. Spacesuits</em>, 2nd ed., Springer Praxis, 2012</li>
      <li>NASA Office of Inspector General — EVA Suit Reports 2017, 2021, 2025</li>
      <li>NASA Safety Message — EVA-23 Water Intrusion Investigation</li>
      <li>NASA Technical Reports Server — Apollo, Gemini, Shuttle program documentation</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 style="font-family:'Bebas Neue',sans-serif;font-size:2rem;letter-spacing:.04em;margin:2.5rem 0 1rem">Created by</h2>
    <p>The Spacesuits is created and developed by <a href="https://metakosmosgroup.com" style="color:var(--cyan)">Metakosmos Group</a> — a space technology company working across product, hardware, software and platforms. For enquiries: <a href="mailto:hello@thespacesuits.com" style="color:var(--cyan)">hello@thespacesuits.com</a></p>
